Subject: [PATCH] fast_lio: publish the IESKF state velocity in nav_msgs/Odometry.twist

Applied by ../Dockerfile with `patch -p1 --forward` inside src/fast_lio, and
asserted immediately afterwards with `grep -q 'twist.twist.linear'
src/laserMapping.cpp` — a patch that silently fails to apply is exactly how you
ship a build that succeeds and a Nav2 that believes the robot never moves.

WHY THIS EXISTS
FAST-LIO2's publish_odometry() sets pose and pose.covariance and never touches
twist (grep 'twist' in the stock ROS2 laserMapping.cpp: 0 hits). Nav2's
controller_server reads the robot's ACTUAL velocity from exactly that field
(nav_2d_utils::OdomSubscriber), so left at zero DWB samples a velocity space
anchored at standstill on every cycle.

WHY NOT DIFFERENTIATE THE POSE
nav_msgs/Odometry.twist is specified in child_frame_id.  Differencing world
poses yields a WORLD-frame velocity; written unrotated into a child_frame_id
field it is correct only when the robot faces +x and is swapped/sign-flipped at
90/180 degrees of yaw.  That is a silent, heading-dependent sign bug that reads
as "the controller is unstable".  Differentiating 10 Hz poses on a biped and
then low-passing away the bandwidth is also the wrong signal to begin with.

WHAT THIS DOES INSTEAD
Publishes the filter's own IESKF state velocity — state_point.vel, already
IMU-fused at 200 Hz — rotated out of the world frame into the body frame with
state_point.rot.conjugate().  Angular velocity comes from the last IMU sample of
the current measurement group minus the estimated gyro bias; the gyro is already
in the body frame, so it needs no rotation.

WHERE IT GOES, AND WHY THAT IS NOT ARBITRARY
The insertion is ABOVE `pubOdomAftMapped->publish(odomAftMapped)`. Upstream
publishes the message and only then fills pose.covariance, so anything written
after that call lands in the NEXT message rather than this one. (That is an
upstream bug in its own right — the published covariance is always one cycle
stale — but it is not ours to fix here.)

SYMBOLS THIS RELIES ON, ALL VERIFIED AGAINST THE PINNED BRANCH
  state_ikfom state_point   laserMapping.cpp:135
  MeasureGroup Measures     laserMapping.cpp:133
  ((SO3, rot)) ((vect3, vel)) ((vect3, bg))   include/use-ikfom.hpp:14,17,18
  deque<sensor_msgs::msg::Imu::ConstSharedPtr> imu   include/common_lib.h:63

MAINTENANCE NOTE: this hunk was GENERATED against hku-mars/FAST_LIO branch ROS2
(FASTLIO_REF in ../Dockerfile), not hand-written — an earlier hand-written
version was rejected because upstream's signature is `SharedPtr pubOdomAftMapped`
rather than `SharedPtr &`, and the function had moved from 618 to 628. Upstream
is not tagged and laserMapping.cpp does move. If `patch --forward` rejects this,
regenerate it against the pinned checkout rather than dropping the change — the
build assertion exists to make that a loud failure, not to be worked around.

--- a/src/laserMapping.cpp
+++ b/src/laserMapping.cpp
@@ -631,6 +631,35 @@
     odomAftMapped.child_frame_id = "body";
     odomAftMapped.header.stamp = get_ros_time(lidar_end_time);
     set_posestamp(odomAftMapped.pose);
+
+    // C3PO: fill twist, which upstream leaves at zero (grep 'twist' in the
+    // stock file: 0 hits). Nav2's controller_server reads the robot's ACTUAL
+    // velocity from this field via nav_2d_utils::OdomSubscriber, so left at
+    // zero DWB samples a velocity space anchored at standstill every cycle.
+    //
+    // Odometry.twist is specified in child_frame_id ("body"), so the world-
+    // frame IESKF state velocity is rotated INTO the body frame - hence the
+    // conjugate. Do NOT replace this with a pose derivative: differencing
+    // world poses gives a world-frame velocity, and writing that unrotated
+    // into a child_frame_id field is correct only when the robot faces +x and
+    // is swapped/sign-flipped at 90/180 degrees of yaw.
+    //
+    // This MUST stay above the publish() below. Upstream publishes before it
+    // fills pose.covariance, so anything written after that call lands in the
+    // NEXT message, not this one.
+    V3D vel_body(state_point.rot.conjugate() * state_point.vel);
+    odomAftMapped.twist.twist.linear.x = vel_body(0);
+    odomAftMapped.twist.twist.linear.y = vel_body(1);
+    odomAftMapped.twist.twist.linear.z = vel_body(2);
+    // The gyro is already a body-frame rate; only the estimated bias comes off.
+    if (!Measures.imu.empty())
+    {
+        const auto &gyr = Measures.imu.back()->angular_velocity;
+        odomAftMapped.twist.twist.angular.x = gyr.x - state_point.bg(0);
+        odomAftMapped.twist.twist.angular.y = gyr.y - state_point.bg(1);
+        odomAftMapped.twist.twist.angular.z = gyr.z - state_point.bg(2);
+    }
+
     pubOdomAftMapped->publish(odomAftMapped);
     auto P = kf.get_P();
     for (int i = 0; i < 6; i ++)
